  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On the sixty-eighth floor of Eighty-Eight True Yang Building, against wind scythe birds, he pours primeval essence into the Gu worms in his hands. Flames clad his body, then split off as a ten metre bronze ape made entirely of fire. The flaming bronze ape has an ugly appearance, teeth like a gorilla, strange horns, and bulging muscles. That form is the flame demon.",
      "chapters": [
        604
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "house_eighty_eight_true_yang_building",
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "It rises into the sky and ignites wind scythe birds that collide with it. Birds along its path roast and fall. He then sheds more flames and forms further copies until six flame demons are on the field and the fire on his body goes out. Fang Yuan judges that the flame demon has great strength. In terms of power the move is on par with dark vortex. The six rampage for an hour as their strength falls, then perish among the birds.",
      "chapters": [
        604
      ],
